{"model":"devstral-small-2:24b-instruct-2512-q4_K_M","created_at":"2026-08-11T18:12:04.9562385Z","response":"# Design Specification for RISC-V Instruction Decoding\n\n## Overview\nThis specification documents the design of a RISC-V instruction decoding system implemented in C++. The code provides structures and methods to parse, validate, and debug RISC-V machine instructions.\n\n## Core Components\n\n### 1. Basic Types and Constants\n\n#### `Instruction` Type\n- **Type**: `unsigned int`\n- **Purpose**: Represents a raw RISC-V instruction word (32 bits)\n\n#### `Immediate` Type\n- **Type**: Not explicitly defined in the code, but used as part of `InstructionBase`\n- **Purpose**: Represents immediate values for various instruction formats\n\n### 2. InstructionBase Structure\n\n#### Fields\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `opcode` | `unsigned` | Operation code (7 bits) |\n| `rs1`, `rs2`, `rd` | `unsigned` | Source/destination registers (5 bits each) |\n| `funct3`, `funct7` | `unsigned` | Function codes (3 and 7 bits respectively) |\n| `imm` | `Immediate` | Immediate value (format varies by instruction type) |\n| `inst` | `Instruction` | Raw instruction word |\n| `t` | `Type` enum | Instruction format type |\n\n#### Type Enum\n```cpp\nenum Type {\n    R, I, S, B, U, J\n};\n```\n- **R**: Register instructions (e.g., ADD)\n- **I**: Immediate instructions (e.g., ADDI)\n- **S**: Store instructions (e.g., SW)\n- **B**: Branch instructions (e.g., BEQ)\n- **U**: Upper immediate instructions (e.g., LUI)\n- **J**: Jump instructions (e.g., JAL)\n\n#### Methods\n\n##### Constructor\n```cpp\nInstructionBase()  // Default constructor initializes all fields to 0\nInstructionBase(unsigned)  // Special constructor for NOP instruction\n```\n\n##### Static Utility Functions\n```cpp\nstatic constexpr unsigned int bin_mask(int digits)\nstatic unsigned int get_digits(unsigned int n, int hi, int lo)\nstatic unsigned int expand_digit(unsigned int digit, int lo)\n```\n\n##### Validation Methods\n```cpp\nbool is_valid(const std::string \u0026key)  // Checks if field access is valid for instruction type\nvoid verify(const std::string \u0026key)    // Throws exception if access would be invalid\n```\n\n##### Debugging Method\n```cpp\nvoid debug()  // Prints human-readable representation of instruction\n```\n\n##### Type Checking Methods\n```cpp\nbool has_op1()   // Returns true if instruction uses rs1\nbool has_op2()   // Returns true if instruction uses rs2\n```\n\n### 3. Instruction Format Structures\n\n#### InstructionR (Register Format)\n- **Fields**: Inherits all from `InstructionBase`\n- **Purpose**: Decodes R-type instructions (e.g., ADD, SUB)\n\n#### InstructionI (Immediate Format)\n- **Fields**: Inherits all from `InstructionBase`\n- **Purpose**: Decodes I-type instructions (e.g., ADDI, LW)\n\n#### InstructionS (Store Format)\n- **Fields**: Inherits all from `InstructionBase`\n- **Purpose**: Decodes S-type instructions (e.g., SW, SH)\n\n#### InstructionB (Branch Format)\n- **Fields**: Inherits all from `InstructionBase`\n- **Purpose**: Decodes B-type instructions (e.g., BEQ, BNE)\n\n#### InstructionU (Upper Immediate Format)\n- **Fields**: Inherits all from `InstructionBase`\n- **Purpose**: Decodes U-type instructions (e.g., LUI, AUIPC)\n\n#### InstructionJ (Jump Format)\n- **Fields**: Inherits all from `InstructionBase`\n- **Purpose**: Decodes J-type instructions (e.g., JAL, JALR)\n\n## Implementation Details\n\n### Field Extraction\nAll instruction format structures extract fields using the same bit manipulation pattern:\n1. Extract opcode from bits [6:0]\n2. Extract register fields from their respective positions\n3. Construct immediate value according to format-specific rules\n\n### Immediate Value Construction\nEach instruction type constructs its immediate value differently:\n- **R-type**: No immediate (field unused)\n- **I-type**: Sign-extended 12-bit immediate\n- **S-type**: Complex construction from multiple bit fields\n- **B-type**: Complex construction with special handling for bit[7]\n- **U-type**: 32-bit immediate formed by shifting upper bits\n- **J-type**: Complex construction with special handling for bit[20]\n\n### Special Cases\n1. **NOP Instruction**:\n   - Created via `InstructionBase(0)`\n   - Has special `inst == -1` marker\n   - `is_nop()` method checks this condition\n\n2. **Invalid Access Handling**:\n   - Throws `InvalidAccess` exception when invalid field is accessed for instruction type\n   - Validation performed via `verify()` method\n\n## Usage Pattern\n\n```cpp\n// Decoding an instruction\nInstruction raw_inst = 0x00A50293; // Example: addi x11, x10, 10\nauto inst = InstructionI(raw_inst); // Create appropriate format object\n\n// Accessing fields (with validation)\ninst.verify(\"rs1\"); // Throws if invalid for this instruction type\nunsigned src_reg = inst.rs1;\n\n// Debugging\ninst.debug(); // Prints human-readable representation\n```\n\n## Dependencies\n- `\u003cutility\u003e`: For general utilities\n- `\"Common.h\"`: Project-specific header (contents not specified)\n- `\u003cstring\u003e`: For string operations in debug output\n- `\u003ciostream\u003e`: For debug output\n\n## Design Considerations\n1. **Type Safety**: Uses `verify()` method to prevent invalid field access\n2. **Extensibility**: Clear structure for adding new instruction formats\n3. **Debugging Support**: Built-in `debug()` method for human-readable output\n4. **NOP Handling**: Special case for NOP instructions with dedicated marker\n\n## Open Questions (Not Specified in Code)\n1. Exact definition of `Immediate` type and its operations\n2. Contents of `\"Common.h\"` header file\n3. Specific behavior of `expand_digit()` function beyond what's shown\n4. Complete list of valid instruction mnemonics for debug output\n\nThis specification provides all necessary information to reimplement the given C++ code while preserving all target-owned identifiers and structure.","done":true,"done_reason":"stop","context":[17,4568,1584,12056,126744,5624,53721,1045,1050,1045,1050,1052,1066,47926,8166,1045,1050,1053,1049,1050,1044,1261,43520,26242,11512,1319,23947,1077,1041,6254,1536,42301,2784,26554,1044,1261,8689,53862,3518,125609,1294,6993,1626,4568,4053,1420,26554,27089,4418,2301,38680,1626,16994,7807,4469,1486,3804,12220,1408,1032,1050,1048,1050,1051,1045,1049,1048,1045,1048,1049,1626,1784,3519,5451,1395,1032,1050,1048,1050,1054,1045,1048,1056,1045,1049,1050,1338,7651,1636,6185,1605,5257,2314,2269,3686,1505,2200,1278,3330,1681,4546,10867,2015,6793,43546,1505,4811,2181,1044,1636,4016,2210,1278,5178,12589,1317,15273,1278,3686,1046,5469,1605,89786,1317,2210,12589,26119,2127,1710,5234,1261,2081,18501,1505,7662,4005,1046,3367,1836,11157,12589,1584,5178,1044,2430,11904,3468,1455,1636,2607,2405,1736,1278,3686,1321,10035,6187,2015,7211,1626,5475,1278,3330,1681,4098,1395,1605,6133,1044,61103,1044,1505,3120,1605,5234,6171,5315,1394,1636,1317,32181,4832,1278,4098,1044,1636,1653,1605,3352,1317,4832,1494,3169,5109,1321,1636,6153,4237,1278,3330,1317,38695,2034,4546,1319,1101,3596,1046,1429,7493,1584,2269,3683,40378,3879,1639,10555,2297,1429,17507,1584,1636,10555,1505,1429,7651,1395,1278,4275,18034,1317,23286,1034,2297,1429,17507,1653,1636,10601,1562,10555,4342,4568,1584,5282,3435,41132,1556,1317,18814,1044,1294,4369,1636,3352,1317,18507,18814,1319,1101,3596,1046,1429,1121,32430,1034,1395,1032,1050,1048,1050,1054,1045,1048,1056,1045,1049,1049,1041,1321,2200,6136,2314,3686,1513,4811,18814,1044,1636,89782,3686,1455,1395,1513,3866,5451,1626,4568,2685,2576,15776,1294,1747,18085,1044,1321,5282,9148,1317,1278,3330,1294,1278,7278,2127,2210,1505,4546,1626,12961,14275,12293,1278,28946,1455,1636,1736,1338,1035,1488,34112,1398,4755,20266,9774,7236,36967,1085,15749,1083,1267,4568,6560,3142,2258,7430,6123,1505,4731,18259,1317,3432,76064,1044,14440,6704,1046,3367,1494,7444,2479,1278,3330,1395,39322,1636,1317,1653,1878,1044,1636,38695,1278,8516,1321,4237,1278,3330,1317,9441,3194